            <ArticleTitle>Practical pearls for oral procedures.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>440-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.clindermatol.2016.02.016</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0738-081X(16)30048-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We provide an overview of clinically relevant principles of oral surgical procedures required in the workup and management of oral mucosal diseases. An understanding of the fundamental concepts of how to perform safely and effectively minor oral procedures is important to the practicing dermatologist and can minimize the need for patient referrals. This chapter reviews the principles of minor oral procedures, including incisional, excisional, and punch biopsies, as well as minor salivary gland excision. Pre- and postoperative patient care is also discussed.</AbstractText>
